{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfvaghs9r42WV3znL5beb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Recommendation: don't run the price survey. Treat this as a failed test and find out why buyers asked for refunds.\n\n**What the numbers show**\n- About 60 of the 20,000 customers bought, and about 24 of those asked for refunds. That leaves roughly 36 retained buyers, or **0.18%**. The target was 3%, so the result is about 17 times short.\n- Even with only 60 buyers, the result is clearly below target. The 95% range for take-up is about 0.23% to 0.39%, so sampling noise doesn't explain the gap.\n- To reach the target, a lower price would need to raise sales more than tenfold. At £5 a month you'd need about 9% take-up just to match the revenue of the original 3% target at £15. A price cut almost never does that.\n- **The refund rate is the most important number.** 40% of the people who did buy it changed their minds once they'd used it. That points to the product not delivering enough value, not to the price being too high. Making it cheaper won't fix that.\n\n**Why the survey won't answer the question**\n- People are poor at predicting whether they would buy at a hypothetical price, and they tend to say yes more often than they actually buy. The survey would produce an encouraging number that you can't trust.\n- It asks the wrong group. The non-buyers already gave you their answer by not buying.\n\n**What I'd do instead**\n1. **Talk to the ~60 buyers, especially the ~24 who asked for refunds.** Ask what they expected and what fell short. This is the cheapest and most useful thing you can learn now.\n2. **Compare the test group with the control group** on churn, satisfaction and standard support contacts. Check that the offer didn't make customers feel the standard support was being held back.\n3. **Pause the add-on.** Only test pricing again if step 1 shows a value problem you can fix. If you do, run a real randomised test with different prices rather than a survey."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3189,"cache_read_input_tokens":5010,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3189},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"82835796-4919-4bb1-8313-8a8dee7b4dcb","uuid":"60fee9a0-5dd8-4eb4-8f0d-cecafbd9c305","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:08:50.958Z","request_id":"req_011CfvaghanTLL5NZJs3B879"}
